## ✅ THE SOLUTION: PRODUCT-INTEGRATED CO-PILOT PAGES

### Architecture Changes:

#### 1. **Add "Powered By" Section to Each Co-Pilot Page**

**New Section Structure:**
```typescript
interface ProductIntegration {
  engines: {
    oracle: {
      apis: string[];           // e.g., ["/predict_variant_impact", "/predict_gene_essentiality"]
      capabilities: string[];   // e.g., ["Sequence analysis", "Pathway mapping"]
      link: "/products/oracle";
    };
    forge?: {
      apis: string[];
      capabilities: string[];
      link: "/products/forge";
    };
    boltz?: {
      apis: string[];
      capabilities: string[];
      link: "/products/boltz";
    };
    commandCenter?: {
      capabilities: string[];
      link: "/products/command-center";
    };
  };
  workflow: {
    steps: Array<{
      step: number;
      title: string;
      engine: "oracle" | "forge" | "boltz" | "commandCenter";
      api?: string;
      description: string;
    }>;
  };
}
```

#### 2. **Update Co-Pilot Data Structure**

**New Field in `CoPilotDetailContent`:**
```typescript
productIntegration?: {
  engines: ProductIntegration['engines'];
  workflow: ProductIntegration['workflow'];
  saeEnabled: boolean;           // Does this use SAE explainability?
  speFramework: {
    sequence: {
      engine: "oracle";
      api: "/predict_variant_impact";
      description: string;
    };
    pathway: {
      engine: "oracle";
      api: "/predict_gene_essentiality";
      description: string;
    };
    evidence: {
      engine: "commandCenter";
      services: string[];
      description: string;
    };
  };
}
```

#### 3. **Create Product Integration Component**

**New Component: `ProductIntegrationSection.tsx`**

**Features:**
- Shows product badges (Oracle, Forge, Boltz, Command Center)
- Visual workflow diagram showing which product powers which step
- Links to product pages
- Shows API endpoints used
- Explains S/P/E framework with product mapping

